Unless I'm completely screwing something up, it's deducing the _negation_ of a
premise from the _negation_ of a consequence, which is perfectly valid logic.
It's called "modus tollens" or the "rule of the contrapositive".

What about "artificial" in the title? Should I not say it there? It is one
thing that makes this project different from most other NLP research.

